From: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: clear the ring to queue map on reset

edma_cfg_rx_desc_rings_reset_queue_mapping() is called before the Rx
rings are configured and to unwind a failed mapping, and its error
string says it unmaps the rings to disable their backpressure
configuration.  It passes the same queue list that the mapping path
passes, so every entry it is meant to withdraw is written again and
nothing is cleared.

Map no queues instead, which writes an empty queue bitmap.  Document
that contract on ppe_edma_ring_to_queues_config(), whose loop over
@queues does not run when @num is zero.  This clears the ten bitmap
words the driver programs; the remaining words of the 64-byte entry are
not written by any code in this driver.

The unwind that calls this from the mapping path tests its return value
inverted, so it reports an error when the reset succeeds and stays quiet
when it fails.  The return value is also held in a u32 while the
function returns a negative errno.

rx_queues[] has no remaining users.  It was a non-static global that
belonged to this file.

Signed-off-by: Francois Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_cfg_rx.c
@@ -32,8 +32,6 @@
 /* EDMA Queue ID to Ring ID Table. */
 #define EDMA_QID2RID_TABLE_MEM(q)	(0xb9000 + (0x4 * (q)))
 
-int rx_queues[] = {0, 8, 16, 24};
-
 static u32 edma_rx_ring_queue_map[][EDMA_MAX_CORE] = {{ 0, 8, 16, 24 },
 						{ 1, 9, 17, 25 },
 						{ 2, 10, 18, 26 },
@@ -49,7 +47,8 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_desc_rings_reset_
 {
 	struct edma_hw_info *hw_info = edma_ctx->hw_info;
 	struct edma_ring_info *rx = hw_info->rx;
-	u32 i, ret;
+	u32 i;
+	int ret;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < rx->num_rings; i++) {
 		struct edma_rxdesc_ring *rxdesc_ring;
@@ -57,7 +56,7 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_desc_rings_reset_
 		rxdesc_ring = &edma_ctx->rx_rings[i];
 
 		ret = ppe_edma_ring_to_queues_config(edma_ctx->ppe_dev, rxdesc_ring->ring_id,
-						     ARRAY_SIZE(rx_queues), rx_queues);
+						     0, NULL);
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("Error in unmapping rxdesc ring %d to PPE queue mapping to disable its backpressure configuration\n",
 			       i);
@@ -143,7 +142,7 @@ static int edma_cfg_rx_desc_ring_to_queu
 		if (ret) {
 			pr_err("Error in configuring Rx ring to PPE queue mapping, ret: %d, id: %d\n",
 			       ret, rxdesc_ring->ring_id);
-			if (!edma_cfg_rx_desc_rings_reset_queue_mapping())
+			if (edma_cfg_rx_desc_rings_reset_queue_mapping())
 				pr_err("Error in resetting Rx desc ring configurations\n");
 
 			return ret;
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_api.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_api.c
@@ -92,11 +92,12 @@ int ppe_edma_queue_resource_get(struct p
  * ppe_edma_ring_to_queues_config - Configure EDMA ring to queue mapping in PPE
  * @ppe_dev: PPE device
  * @ring_id: EDMA ring ID
- * @num: Number of queues mapped to EDMA ring
- * @queues: PPE queue IDs
+ * @num: Number of queues mapped to EDMA ring, zero to map none
+ * @queues: PPE queue IDs, not accessed when @num is zero
  *
  * Enable EDMA ring to PPE queue mapping configuration for packet
- * receive to an EDMA ring.
+ * receive to an EDMA ring.  Mapping zero queues writes an empty queue
+ * bitmap, which leaves no queue associated with the ring.
  *
  * Return 0 on success, negative error code on failure.
  */
